From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 05 Nov 2026 22:43:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-ipq8074: add port 5 UNIPHY1 SGMII rates

Port 5 can use either UNIPHY0 or UNIPHY1. Its 25 MHz and 125 MHz
configurations currently cover UNIPHY0 in SGMII mode and UNIPHY1 in
SGMII+ mode, but omit UNIPHY1 in SGMII mode.

With UNIPHY0 unavailable and UNIPHY1 supplying 125 MHz, the closest
125 MHz configuration divides UNIPHY1 by 2.5 and actually supplies
50 MHz. An AP8220 negotiated at 1 Gbps reports this clock rate together
with zero good RX packets, MAC alignment errors and HPPE CRC-error drops.
The 25 MHz configuration has the corresponding missing divide-by-5 case.

Append the SGMII divisors for RX and TX, retaining the existing SGMII+
and UNIPHY0 alternatives and their priority when more than one parent
can supply a matching rate. Leave the 2.5 Gbps rate and port 6 unchanged.

Signed-off-by: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq8074.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq8074.c
@@ -1680,11 +1680,13 @@ static struct clk_regmap_div nss_port4_t
 static const struct freq_conf ftbl_nss_port5_rx_clk_src_25[] = {
 	C(P_UNIPHY1_RX, 12.5, 0, 0),
 	C(P_UNIPHY0_RX, 5, 0, 0),
+	C(P_UNIPHY1_RX, 5, 0, 0),
 };
 
 static const struct freq_conf ftbl_nss_port5_rx_clk_src_125[] = {
 	C(P_UNIPHY1_RX, 2.5, 0, 0),
 	C(P_UNIPHY0_RX, 1, 0, 0),
+	C(P_UNIPHY1_RX, 1, 0, 0),
 };
 
 static const struct freq_multi_tbl ftbl_nss_port5_rx_clk_src[] = {
@@ -1750,11 +1752,13 @@ static struct clk_regmap_div nss_port5_r
 static const struct freq_conf ftbl_nss_port5_tx_clk_src_25[] = {
 	C(P_UNIPHY1_TX, 12.5, 0, 0),
 	C(P_UNIPHY0_TX, 5, 0, 0),
+	C(P_UNIPHY1_TX, 5, 0, 0),
 };
 
 static const struct freq_conf ftbl_nss_port5_tx_clk_src_125[] = {
 	C(P_UNIPHY1_TX, 2.5, 0, 0),
 	C(P_UNIPHY0_TX, 1, 0, 0),
+	C(P_UNIPHY1_TX, 1, 0, 0),
 };
 
 static const struct freq_multi_tbl ftbl_nss_port5_tx_clk_src[] = {
